@NVIDIA/mcore-oncall — production forward/backward parity is now complete on head `caee7ca7fecf68b5b086953209a3f902dc3ed5f2` across 8×B200.

The run exercised the actual `MambaLayer -> MambaMixer -> ssd_combined` CUDA path with recompute disabled versus `recompute_modules=["mamba"]`, restoring identical RNG immediately before each forward. All 8 ranks passed with 0 skips/failures; outputs, input gradients, and all 12 parameter gradients had max absolute and relative difference `0`, with no NaN/Inf/OOM. `causal-conv1d==1.7.0` was importable and its fused forward callable was active. The source tree was clean and the distributed command exited 0.

This closes the production-parity follow-up from my previous comment. Could you route this for review and `/ok to test caee7ca7fecf68b5b086953209a3f902dc3ed5f2`?

@jiemingz @dimapihtar CI for `6f88cf61288ae4d31c3c9211a0c2b625ab7c2e4d` has passed, including all 12 Mamba recompute cases and the H100 integration jobs. The SSM bucket passed 387 tests with 9 skips.

The remaining red checks require owner approvals: `mamba_layer.py` lists `core-adlr`, `core-nemo`, and `hybrid-model`; `transformer_config.py` lists `core-adlr`, `core-nemo`, and `transformer`. Could you review the Mamba integration and help route those approvals?

